==============================================================================
V5  demand D(g) vs transposition length L(g)
==============================================================================
    D(g) = min over the faithful reps available to the layer of
           rank(rho(g) - I).  L(g) is what our oracle currently charges.

    S3   |G|=  6  min faithful dim 2   max D = 2  (max L = 2)
          L=0:D=0   L=1:D=1   L=2:D=2
          demand over non-identity elements: [1, 2]   varies: True

    S4   |G|= 24  min faithful dim 3   max D = 3  (max L = 3)
          L=0:D=0   L=1:D=1   L=2:D=2   L=3:D=3
          demand over non-identity elements: [1, 2, 3]   varies: True

    A4   |G|= 12  min faithful dim 3   max D = 2  (max L = 2)
          L=0:D=0   L=2:D=2
          demand over non-identity elements: [2]   varies: False   <-- adaptivity cannot help here

    A5   |G|= 60  min faithful dim 3   max D = 2  (max L = 4)  <-- D < L
          L=0:D=0   L=2:D=2   L=4:D=2
          demand over non-identity elements: [2]   varies: False   <-- adaptivity cannot help here

    S5   |G|=120  min faithful dim 4   max D = 4  (max L = 4)
          L=0:D=0   L=1:D=1   L=2:D=2   L=3:D=3   L=4:D=4
          demand over non-identity elements: [1, 2, 3, 4]   varies: True

==============================================================================
WHAT THIS CHANGES
==============================================================================
  1. Our oracle charges L(g). That is correct for S5 -- in the
     4-dimensional standard rep, rank(rho(g) - I) = L(g) exactly --
     so the p = 0.05 / 0.1 / 0.25 results stand as measured.

  2. It is WRONG for A5. At p = 1.0 the alphabet is 24 five-cycles,
     which generate A5, where every element costs 2. The oracle
     charged 4. The 'negative control' fired for the right reason
     (no gap at p=1) but with the wrong number, and fixed n_h=3
     solving the task is the tell.

  3. The demand is a property of the ALPHABET, not the token. That
     is the testable prediction: add one transposition to a 5-cycle
     alphabet -- the cheapest token there is -- and every 5-cycle
     goes from costing 2 to costing 4.

  4. And it bounds our own mechanism honestly: where D is constant
     across the group (A5), adaptive order cannot help at all. Where
     D varies (S5), it can. We can now predict which before running.
==============================================================================

